**Code Explanation:**

The code loads the five provided CSV datasets (returns.csv, factors.csv, true_betas.csv, market_cap.csv, and book_to_market.csv) from the absolute path /home/node/work/projects/equity_factors_v1/ and ensures their indices are properly formatted as datetime objects. It then performs a 36-month rolling Ordinary Least Squares (OLS) regression to estimate the market beta for each of the 50 stocks. For each month t starting from the 37th month (index 36), the beta is calculated using the covariance between the stock returns and the market factor (MKT_RF) over the preceding 36 months, divided by the variance of the market factor over the same window. Using these out-of-sample beta estimates, the code computes the out-of-sample residuals for months 37–120 by subtracting the product of the estimated beta and the realized market return from the actual stock return. Finally, all the original data, along with the newly computed residuals and estimated betas, are consolidated into a single dictionary and saved as a pickle file (data/consolidated_data.pkl) for efficient loading in subsequent steps.

