**Code Explanation:**

The code computes the annualized Information Ratio (IR) and performs a variance-based decomposition for three types of portfolios: OLS-FMP (Naive), OLS-FMP (Ledoit-Wolf), and Neutralized Characteristic-Sorted (NCS) portfolios. 1. Data Loading & Setup: It loads the consolidated dataset, including returns, true betas, factors, market capitalization, and residuals. It also loads the pre-computed NCS portfolio returns from Step 4. 2. OLS-FMP Construction across N: For each cross-sectional sample size N in [10, 50], it selects stocks by ranking their true SMB and HML betas. It then computes the portfolio weights using both a Naive (Identity) covariance matrix and a Ledoit-Wolf shrinkage covariance matrix fitted on the full 120-month return sample. 3. Performance Metrics (IR): Using the out-of-sample period (months 37-120), it calculates the annualized IR for the SMB and WML factors for both OLS-FMP variants. The NCS portfolio IR is also computed over the same period. 4. Variance Decomposition: It isolates the Factor Component (R_projected) by projecting the portfolio weights onto the true factor returns (W * B * f). The Noise Component (R_noise) is the residual portfolio return not explained by the true factors. The variance decomposition ratio (Var(R_projected) / Var(R_noise)) is computed to quantify the signal-to-noise ratio. 5. Visualization & Output: A two-panel figure is generated to compare the IR decay profiles of the low-Sharpe (SMB) and high-Sharpe (WML) factors across N. Finally, the variance decomposition ratios and annualized IRs at specific thresholds (N=10, 25, 50) are printed to the console.

